A line saying user 7 sent PATCH to `/accounts/5` doesn't say the billing email changed from X to Y. If you need that history for billing-email changes and deletions, write an audit row in the same SQL statement as the update. A CTE lets `write()` keep running a single statement. Don't put that history in request logs, since it would mean logging PII.

